<title>JAPAN: Mitsui Trust forgives loans to mortgage firms.</title>
<headline>Mitsui Trust forgives loans to mortgage firms.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsui Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd said on Monday that it had forgiven loans totalling 223.2 billion yen which it had extended to two mortgage firms.</p>
<p>The company forgave loans worth 185.6 billion yen and 37.7 billion yen to Juso Inc and Nippon Housing Loan Co Ltd respectively, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Mitsui Trust also said forgiving these loans to the mortgage firms would not affect the company's forecast for its earnings for the current 1996/97 business year ending on March 31.</p>
</text>
